NOTE: the incumbent 4-cycle baseline is safe at skin temperature in all 5 conditions. It is conservative, not unsafe: it leaves margin on the table rather than crossing the limit.
      Optimiser raises cycles 4 -> 4.8 in every condition (the chemistry constraint boundary), and moves the fan DOWN in 4 of 5 conditions and UP in 1.
      Fan speed is not a free lever: lowering it saves fan power and evaporation but raises entering condenser water. Across the 5 surviving conditions
      the optimum tops out at 34.5 degC. The binding limit is the chiller's CAPACITY, not its 35 degC temperature ceiling: above about 32.5 degC
      the machine cannot make the duty at all. Not tower physics and not chemistry -- that is the coupling this product exists to price.

